n to your version of the file, but you are not obligated to do so. \r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/964438702/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/964439798","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1356#issuecomment-964439798","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1356","id":964439798,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE845fC72","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-11-09T18:55:00Z","updated_at":"2021-11-09T18:55:00Z","body":"3. is the omission or inclusion of the last line of the second paragraph, substantively different? (line in italics is sometimes present and sometimes missing)\r\n\r\n\"You must obey the GNU General Public License in all respects for all of the code used other than OpenSSL.  \r\nIf you modify file(s) with this exception, you may extend this exception to your version of the file(s), but you are not obligated to do so.  \r\nIf you do not wish to do so, delete this exception statement from your version. \r\n_If you delete this exception statement from all source files in the program, then also delete it here._\"","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/964439798/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/964441540","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1356#issuecomment-964441540","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1356","id":964441540,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE845fDXE","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-11-09T18:56:14Z","updated_at":"2021-11-09T18:56:14Z","body":"there is also an exception that applies to the LGPL - so that will surely need its own exception. \r\n\r\nlegal team - please comment separately on each numbered question (and identify which one)!\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/964441540/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/971060655","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1356#issuecomment-971060655","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1356","id":971060655,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE8454TWv","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-11-17T01:42:53Z","updated_at":"2021-11-17T01:42:53Z","body":"@jlovejoy Thanks for organizing all of this and getting the conversation moving forward!\r\n\r\nHere are my gut reactions to your questions. I don't have strong feelings on them and could be persuaded otherwise.\r\n\r\n### Responding to [question 1](https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1356#issuecomment-964437122):\r\n\r\nI feel pretty comfortable considering these two to be equivalent for SPDX ID purposes:\r\n\r\n* the code of this program with the OpenSSL Library (or with modified versions of OpenSSL that use the same license as OpenSSL),\r\n* this program with the OpenSSL library (or with modified versions of OpenSSL that use the same license as OpenSSL),\r\n\r\nThose two are identical other than \"code of this program\" vs. \"program\" -- I think that's substantively identical.\r\n\r\nThe following two I feel less comfortable considering to be equivalent to the above (or to each other):\r\n* the code of this program with any version of the OpenSSL library which is distributed under a license identical to that listed in the included COPYING.OpenSSL file,\r\n* the code of portions of this program with the OpenSSL library under certain conditions as described in each individual source file,\r\n\r\nThat's because both of these punt on which other license needs to be matched, for the first one whatever is in \"the included COPYING.OpenSSL file\" and for the second whatever \"certain conditions\" are \"described in each individual source file.\"\r\n\r\n### Responding to [question 2](https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1356#issuecomment-964438702):\r\n\r\nSo, unlike my response to 1, for these I actually feel fine treating these as equivalent.\r\n\r\nI tend to distinguish (A) changes that might modify the effect of the license or exception, vs. (B) changes that might modify knowing which software or other content the license or exception applies to.\r\n\r\nQuestion 1 is about changes of type A: it modifies what the effect of the exception is. Question 2 is about changes of type B: it's just about knowing which files the exception applies to.\r\n\r\nGiven that, I tend to think that for question 2, we treat changes of this type as equivalent, and it would be a matter of e.g. whoever is creating an SPDX document to determine which files they're going to say are under this license ID.\r\n\r\n### Responding to [question 3](https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1356#issuecomment-964439798)\r\n\r\nThis is about the line: _\"If you delete this exception statement from all source files in the program, then also delete it here.\"_\r\n\r\nPersonally I feel like this is not about the license / exception itself -- more about how to apply the license / exception to your work. (Or, more precisely, how to _not_ apply the exception to your work...)\r\n\r\nI'd compare this more to something like the \"appendix\" language at the end of licenses like Apache-2.0 or GPL-2.0. I think we typically treat those as optional, so I'd also lean towards saying that it should be treated as equivalent whether or not this line is present.\r\n\r\n## Responding to [comment about LGPL](https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1356#issuecomment-964441540)\r\n\r\nugh\r\n\r\nhow would we feel about making the portion of the exception that names the license, into replaceable text? And/or, just making \"Lesser\" into optional text there?\r\n\r\nSince it's an exception, in any case where it's used it's going to be including the appropriate license as part of the license expression. E.g., `GPL-2.0-or-later WITH Whatever-OpenSSL-exception` -- so could we just match the exception text itself without caring which license is named within the exception's text?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/971060655/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/990092029","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1356#issuecomment-990092029","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1356","id":9900